removal retry budget (REMOVAL_BACKOFFS, sum ~1.9s) that re-issues the DELETE when the tree comes back, instead of reporting the race as a leak on the first attempt. Proved hermetically in tests/test_teardown_resilience.py (4 tests: recreated twice is still removed; always-recreated is reported and bounded; a refused DELETE still keeps directory+row per AUG-117; a real namespace name is refused), now named in tests/gate.sh's pytest arm. DuckBrain-side root cause (indexer must cancel or await pending writes on delete) is filed against DuckBrain.", "review_notes": null, "source": null, "status": "complete", "title": "Namespace teardown fails when a concurrent indexer recreates the directory (ENOTEMPTY)", "ts": null, "updated_at": "2026-11-09T23:30:27.45227+00:00"}
