+ {"status": "complete", "id": "AUG-132", "title": "[P1] spec validate reports ok for a corpus whose test reference points at a file that does not exist", "detail": {"fingerprint": "30f14fd9761b4ab21fadc999cb213dbd5ca6e6a56bb113240ecc1499d20213da", "evidence": [{"run_id":"083a34e6","ts":"2026-11-09T18:01:39.614415+00:00","tree_fp":"b2ba30e2248c64b2def53a2d245cefe5894d15913513467ae3595481f28e9b69"}]}, "priority": "P1", "source": null, "reasoning": "Dogfood spike /tmp/auger_dogfood_spike.py: a spec pointing at tests/does-not-exist.py with a bogus selector returned rc=0 and 'ok'. Same failure class as AUG-123 (obligations that never fire) and AUG-130 (gate passes with the arm skipped): verification that reports success without checking the thing it exists to check. (Re-created after I discarded the row with an over-broad 'git checkout -- .coding-hermes/board/' during the landing cleanup.)", "review_notes": null, "ts": null, "acceptance_criteria": "A corpus whose verification block names tests/does-not-exist.py with any selector must make 'auger spec validate' exit non-zero and print the offending document, block and resolved path. Today the same corpus prints 'spec: 1 document(s), 2 block(s), 1 reference(s) ok' and exits 0 (measured 2026-11-03), so the command validates counts, not obligations. A committed fixture under tests/fixtures/xml/ reproduces it, the assertion runs inside the gate's pytest arm, and the fixed command still exits 0 on the shipped valid corpus.", "complexity": 3, "created_at": "2026-11-04T00:38:31.92035+00:00", "updated_at": "2026-11-09T18:01:55.525862+00:00", "foreman_note": "DUPLICATE of AUG-128 (evidence recorded, closure pending the fix run id). Probe /home/kara/.hermes/cache/scratch/dor_method_vs_type.py against auger.validate_xml_specs, shipped fixture tests/fixtures/xml/verification/migration.xml, only the path changed to tests/does-not-exist.py: (A) type=test -> refused stale-test-ref TEST-MIG-1; (B) method=test -> validator returned OK (the bug); (C) method=test as shipped -> OK. The obligation gate was keyed on type alone while the XSD allows both verification and method and every shipped fixture writes method=test. Same root cause as AUG-128, which was already filed with that diagnosis; AUG-128 carries the fix and two tests.\n\nLANDED on main as 55a6725 (ff-merge). Measured by the foreman on the merged tree: 'spec validate tests/fixtures/xml/invalid/stale-test-obligation' -> rc 2 'stale-test-ref: stale-test-obligation.xml: AUG-VER-STALE-1: tests/does-not-exist.py (resolved .../tests/does-not-exist.py)'; shipped corpus still rc 0 ('3 document(s), 10 block(s), 6 reference(s) ok'). Row stays in_progress: closure needs a GitReins verdict bound to 55a6725.\n\nReceipt (folds auto-emitted event 523): complete on judged PASS run 083a34e6 (.gitreins/history/2026-11-09/083a34e6/), task_id=AUG-132, commit=5da5b4a1cdf485ce301d86da47378c7d8b894fb2, passed=true, pass_class=judged, tier2 items 9/9 PASS. Tier1 steps cite the stale guard-20261105T170854 log (AUG-160) but the step OUTPUT is fresh: '== gate mode: FULL gate ==', 717 passed / 2 skipped in 833.80s, wrapper regression (AUG-081) PASS, AUG-130 skipped-arm policy PASS, LIVE ARMS ran 2 skipped 0, GATE PASS. Criteria measured: shipped AUG-132 fixture refused rc 2 stale-test-ref by BOTH verbs; valid corpora rc 0 with unchanged counts (fixtures 3/10/6, specs 3/12/7); out-of-tree mutant of migration.xml refused TEST-MIG-1 while the unmutated control passed; 31 regression tests pass; both files in the gate arm (2 occurrences each) and 55a6725 an ancestor of HEAD.", "commit_hash": "5da5b4a1cdf485ce301d86da47378c7d8b894fb2", "worker_status": "complete", "guard_result": "PASS", "ci_result": "GREEN", "worker_summary": "Landed as 55a6725 (AUG-134+AUG-132: one loader, one verdict; validate now resolves test obligations). Judged PASS: verdict run 083a34e6, task_id=AUG-132, commit=5da5b4a, pass_class=judged; tier1 lint/secrets/tests PASS (real bash tests/gate.sh: 717 pa